/div></div><div class="makeStylesgradeInfo-0-2-663"><div class="makeStylesgradeDetail-0-2-664">Due date: 6/16/26, 1:59 AM (CDT)</div></div><div class="makeStylescontentItemDescriptionContainer-0-2-648 js-description">This week, you’re focusing on the distinctions between facts and opinions, as well as objective versus subjective information. Understanding these differences is crucial for making sense of the information you encounter every day. You will also explore inductive and deductive reasoning, two key methods for building and evaluating arguments. By understanding these concepts, you will improve your critical thinking and decision-making abilities. Let's dive in and see how these ideas apply to real-world situations and your daily life. Discuss the following with the class: Fact vs. Opinion: Think about an article or news story you read recently. Identify one statement of fact and one statement of opinion from the article. How did you ...</div></div><div class="makeStylescontentItemContextArea-0-2-620"><button aria-expanded="false" aria-haspopup="true" aria-label="More options for Wk 3 Discussion: Critical Thinking and Effective Reasoning [due Thurs]" class="MuiButtonBaseroot-0-2-659 MuiIconButtonroot-0-2-650 makeStylesoverflowMenu-0-2-649" data-analytics-id="components.directives.content-item-base.overflowMenu.showMenu.button" id="content-item-overflow-menu-button-_55105957_1" tabindex="0" title="More options for Wk 3 Discussion: Critical Thinking and Effective Reasoning [due Thurs]" type="button"><span class="MuiIconButtonlabel-0-2-658"><svg aria-hidden="true" class="MuiSvgIconroot-0-2-630 makeStylesdirectionalIcon-0-2-629 makeStylesstrokeIcon-0-2-628 MuiSvgIconfontSizeSmall-0-2-637" focusable="false" role="presentation" viewbox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M0 8c0-1.1046.8954-2 2-2s2 .8954 2 2-.8954 2-2 2-2-.8954-2-2zM6 8c0-1.1046.8954-2 2-2s2 .8954 2 2-.8954 2-2 2-2-.8954-2-2zM14 6c-1.1046 0-2 .8954-2 2s.8954 2 2 2 2-.8954 2-2-.8954-2-2-2z" fill="currentColor" str