2-370">Due date: 6/30/26, 1:59 AM (CDT)</div></div><div class="makeStylescontentItemDescriptionContainer-0-2-354 js-description">This week, we are exploring the six thinking hats method, a powerful tool for enhancing critical thinking and problem-solving. By using different "hats" to represent various thinking styles, we can approach challenges from multiple perspectives, leading to more comprehensive and effective solutions. This method encourages collaborative and cooperative thinking, allowing us to explore facts, emotions, risks, benefits, and creative ideas in a structured way. As you engage with this week's discussion questions, think about how you can apply the six thinking hats to real-world problems you have faced. Discuss the following with your classmates: Applying the Six Thinking Hats: Think about a problem or challenge you have faced recently. ...</div></div><div class="makeStylescontentItemContextArea-0-2-326"><button class="MuiButtonBaseroot-0-2-365 MuiIconButtonroot-0-2-356 makeStylesoverflowMenu-0-2-355" tabindex="0" type="button" id="content-item-overflow-menu-button-_55105959_1" title="More options for Wk 5 Discussion: The Six Thinking Hats [due Thurs]" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="More options for Wk 5 Discussion: The Six Thinking Hats [due Thurs]" aria-haspopup="true" data-analytics-id="components.directives.content-item-base.overflowMenu.showMenu.button"><span class="MuiIconButtonlabel-0-2-364"><svg class="MuiSvgIconroot-0-2-336 makeStylesdirectionalIcon-0-2-335 makeStylesstrokeIcon-0-2-334 MuiSvgIconfontSizeSmall-0-2-343" focusable="false" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" role="presentation"><path fill="currentColor" stroke="transparent" d="M0 8c0-1.1046.8954-2 2-2s2 .8954 2 2-.8954 2-2 2-2-.8954-2-2zM6 8c0-1.1046.8954-2 2-2s2 .8954 2 2-.8954 2-2 2-2-.8954-2-2zM14 6c-1.1046 0-2 .8954-2 2s.8954 2 2 2 2-.8954 2-2-.8954-2-2-2z"></path></svg></span></button><div></div></div></div></div></div></div><button class="MuiButtonBaseroot-0-2-3